# Weather and Maps: do the requests these two applications make leave the phone, and what does Apple
# answer? Built with RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.weathermaps (userland/build.sh copies this file to /etc/rc.jobs,
# and the launchd job com.redwood.demo runs it at boot, with its output on the console).
#
# Why this and not the console's silence: /dev/console DROPS LINES (userland/mkjobs.py says so in the
# store-stack note, and net_test's own output went missing in a run whose steps demonstrably ran). So
# "Weather never asked" cannot be concluded from an absent log line -- it has to be measured by asking
# the same questions the applications ask, in the same order, and printing the answers.
#
# The order is the one a stock application goes through: address, name, reachability, then the request.
# bag.itunes.apple.com is the control: TLS to Apple that this image is known to complete (rc.jobs.store).
# weather-data.apple.com is what the Weather app fetches its forecast from; gspe19-ssl.ls.apple.com is
# one of the tile servers GeoServices asks for map tiles. An answer of 200 with data means the network
# and TLS are fine and the gap is in what the app does with it; a 4xx/5xx, or a "x-" header saying the
# request was rejected, means Apple refused it -- which is where signing would show up.

/bin/echo "=== WM: weather and maps, measured ==="
/redwood/bin/net_test waitaddr en0 60
/redwood/bin/net_test show

/bin/echo "=== WM: names ==="
/redwood/bin/net_test resolve weather-data.apple.com
/redwood/bin/net_test resolve gspe19-ssl.ls.apple.com

/bin/echo "=== WM: reachability, what an app asks before it tries ==="
/redwood/bin/net_test reach weather-data.apple.com
/redwood/bin/net_test reach gspe19-ssl.ls.apple.com

/bin/echo "=== WM: control, TLS to Apple that is known to work ==="
/redwood/bin/net_test fetch https://bag.itunes.apple.com/bag.xml

/bin/echo "=== WM: weather data ==="
/redwood/bin/net_test fetch https://weather-data.apple.com/v3/weather/en_US/45.25/19.84

/bin/echo "=== WM: maps tile server ==="
/redwood/bin/net_test fetch https://gspe19-ssl.ls.apple.com/

/bin/echo "=== WM: done ==="
